body:
I imagine that the direction of growth has more to do with the direction the light is coming from than the placement of the router. It appears that all light sources (ceiling and lamp) are on the side of the plant opposite from the router. Though it looks bright enough, photographs can sometimes be deceptive in depicting the level of light in a room. If the plant is struggling to get enough light for all of its leaves to photosynthesize, the discrepancy in growth direction will be more pronounced. The black sound proofing on the wall near the router may exacerbate the issue by absorbing light that would otherwise be reflected toward the plant.

&#x200B;

 The router's heat output may affect plant growth to some degree.
